-- title:
--   Stalk at a node over an intermediate discrete-valuation level
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring such that for all $a,b \in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b \neq 0$ one has $b \mid a^{n}$ for some $n$. Let $F/L$ be an extension which is a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, all residue fields of places are finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$) and essentially of finite type, and let $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ be integral, proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, together with a ring isomorphism $\varphi : F \cong K(X)$ carrying $\operatorname{algebraMap} L F(a)$ to the germ at the generic point of the global section attached to $a \in A$. Assume a descent datum: a discrete valuation ring $A_0$ with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ and an injective local homomorphism $\iota_0 : A_0 \to A$ with every element of $A$ algebraic over the image of $\iota_0$, a model $X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$ (integral, proper, flat, locally of finite presentation) and an isomorphism $X \cong X_0 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_0} \operatorname{Spec} A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $x \in X$ be a closed point (every point to which $x$ specialises equals $x$) lying over the closed point of $A$, and let $\eta_1 \neq \eta_2$ be two points, both distinct from $x$, specialising to $x$, such that any point specialising to $x$, distinct from $x$ and lying over the closed point of $A$, is $\eta_1$ or $\eta_2$; assume further that the subrings $\varphi^{-1}(\mathcal O_{X,\eta_i}) \subseteq F$ are the valuation subrings of regular prolongations $R_i$ of $A$ to $F$ with residue fields $\bar F_i$ over the residue field of $A$. Let $x_0 \in X_0$ be the image of $x$, let $w \geq 1$, and assume a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}$ onto $\widehat{A_0}[[u,v]]/(uv - \varpi_0^{\,w})$ which sends the image of each $a \in A_0$ to the corresponding constant. Finally, let $A_1$ be a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\varpi_1$, equipped with local homomorphisms $\iota_1' : A_0 \to A_1$ and $\iota_1 : A_1 \to A$ with $\iota_1$ injective and $\iota_1 \circ \iota_1' = \iota_0$, let $f_1 : X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and $g_1 : X_1 \to X_0$ form a pullback square over $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_1'$, and let $e_1 : X \cong X_1 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_1} \operatorname{Spec} A$ be an isomorphism over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ whose first projection, followed by $g_1$, agrees with the projection $X \to X_0$. Writing $x_1$ for the image of $x$ in $X_1$, the conclusion is twofold: every $s \in \mathcal O_{X_1,x_1}$ admits $a \in A_1$ with $s$ minus the germ at $x_1$ of the global section of $X_1$ attached to $a$ a non-unit; and $\mathfrak m_{x_1}$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{X_0,g_1(x_1)}$ under the stalk map of $g_1$ and the ideal generated by the germ at $x_1$ of the global section attached to $\varpi_1$.
--
--   This is the local computation at a node of a semistable model after base change to an intermediate discrete-valuation level: the crossing presentation of the completed local ring at $x_0$ forces $x_0$ to be rational over the residue field of $A_0$, so the point $x_1$ of $X_1 = X_0 \times_{A_0} A_1$ above it is unique with residue field that of $A_1$, which is what the two assertions express. It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.stalk_level_of_isPullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.stalk_level_of_isPullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk) in the analysis of the local structure of models of curves over valuation rings.
